  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The American Institute of Applied Sciences in Switzerland (AUS) is one of Switzerland’s leading higher education institutions. It offers bachelor's and master's programs in several specialisations.</p><p>The University’s Master in Management program has been ranked in the QS World University Rankings 2024 as one of the top 150 globally and top 2 in Switzerland.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student life",
      "value": "<p>AUS has students from over 40 nationalities, with around 80% of the student population from overseas, providing a globally diverse learning environment.</p><p>The University has a close-knit faculty-to-student ratio of 1:7 and small class sizes, having a maximum of 20 students per class. This gives you personalised mentorship from professors.</p><p>The University organises numerous events and activities throughout the year. These include activities like skiing, barbeques, movie evenings, and more. You will also have access to a host of brilliant facilities, like lecture theatres, interactive learning spaces, and computer labs to enhance your study experience.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>AUS has several student residences near the campus. The administration team can assist you with finding the right accommodation, on a first-come-first-serve basis. You can also look for alternative accommodation in and around the local area.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Cafeteria",
      "value": "<p>The popular Metropolis Snack Bar at the campus provides hot meals, snacks and refreshments at attractive prices. There are also plenty of restaurants and cafes within walking distance of the campus.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
